<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak c.bank reserves fall to $3.48 bln - Nov 6.</title>
<headline>Slovak c.bank reserves fall to $3.48 bln - Nov 6.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) on Friday said its hard currency reserves fell to $3.483 billion as of November 6, from $3.599 billion on October 29.</p>
<p> HARD CURRENCY RESERVES     Nov 6     Oct 29    Nov '95</p>
<p>  NBS reserves ($bln)	 3.483     3.599     3.046</p>
<p>  Commercial banks	    1.208     1.157     1.590</p>
<p>  Entire banking sector     4.692     4.755     4.636</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3687</p>
